      "side": 1,
      "message": "Just a thought: A malicious host can pass in bad values for irqchip_mode and max_vcpu_ids after the first vCPU is created successfully and fail the subsequent vcpu creations. We could probably avoid this by moving it inside the lock. Not a security issue though, just a DoS like attack. And if a malicious host wants to fail the VM creation there are lot other ways as well, so not really too concerned about it.",
